---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About CyberPulse Intelligence: what the project is, what it publishes and what it does not do yet." path="/about/">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="About CyberPulse Intelligence"
    description="A research publication for cybersecurity analysis, built to show its working: sources, confidence and limits, stated on every page."
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 pb-24 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_20rem]">
      <div class="prose-article">
        <h2>What we publish</h2>
        <p>
          CyberPulse Intelligence publishes written analysis in five areas: latest research, CVE intelligence,
          malware analysis, threat actor profiles and exploit intelligence. Each area is written for people who
          defend systems. Articles explain what is happening, why it matters, and what a team can check or change.
        </p>

        <h2>What we will not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Publish invented statistics, incidents or research findings presented as real.</li>
          <li>Publish working exploit code or step-by-step attack instructions.</li>
          <li>Name individuals in threat actor profiles without a documented public basis.</li>
          <li>Claim attribution with more confidence than the evidence supports.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Current state of the project</h2>
        <p>
          This is the first version of the site. It has no published articles yet, so there are no findings to cite.
          Anything published later will be identified as research, with its sources.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no automatic publishing, no live threat feed, no newsletter service and no analytics connected
          yet. Those are planned and will be added deliberately, with their own review.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact and corrections</h2>
        <p>
          The project source, issue tracker and corrections process live on
          <a href={SITE.repository} rel="noopener" target="_blank">GitHub</a>. Corrections to published research
          are recorded in the article's <em>Updated</em> date.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="space-y-6">
        <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist-300">
          <p class="font-semibold text-white">Stack</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Astro, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS and Markdown content collections, deployed to GitHub Pages with GitHub Actions.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
